{"duration_api_ms":746258,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"8ab6682a-3eba-4ac5-96e7-fb459630bd7b","total_cost_usd":18.919444500000004,"usage":{"input_tokens":200,"cache_creation_input_tokens":193885,"cache_read_input_tokens":26448398,"output_tokens":76593,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":19146},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":193885,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":24084,"cache_read_input_tokens":348135,"cache_creation_input_tokens":23077,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":23077},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5[1m]":{"inputTokens":204,"outputTokens":77299,"thinkingTokens":19318,"cacheReadInputTokens":26547659,"cacheCreationInputTokens":371212,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":18.919444500000004,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":125,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"All 20 findings have fixes in the working tree. `flutter test` passes (44 tests, exit 0). `dart analyze` finds no errors but exits 2 because of 5 unused-import warnings, all in files this pass didn't touch: `http/live.dart`, `http/video.dart`, `pages/audio/view.dart` and two in `pages/mine/controller.dart`. The C++ change for Finding 17 has **not been compiled**, and nothing was run in the app.\n\n## 1. What changed, per finding\n\n1. **`access_key` leak**: after the request interceptor picks the account, any request not bound to a logged-in account has `access_key`/`mobile_access_key` removed from its query and map body. If it was already signed, it is re-signed (every call site uses the default appkey). This covers `liveFeedIndex`, `liveSecondList`, `liveAreaList`, `liveRoomAreaList`, `liveSearch`, `liveFeedback`, `spaceShop`, and any other call site that adds the key.\n2. **gRPC path**: `requiresAccount` strips `HttpString.appBaseUrl` before comparing against the gRPC lists. The test now uses real `appBaseUrl + GrpcUrl.x` paths and adds a `dynRed` case.\n3. **csrf on GET**: the csrf check applies only to non-GET requests. The three csrf tests now set `method: 'POST'`; before, they relied on `RequestOptions` defaulting to GET.\n4. **Logout in incognito**: when a request explicitly passes a `LoginAccount` and its path is `logout`, `activateBuvidApi` or `qrcodeConfirm`, that account is used whatever the mode.\n5. **Roles**:\n   - New `Accounts.savedMode()` builds the roles from the saved accounts. The role dialog now loads from it and compares against it.\n   - `Accounts.set` removes the role from every saved account, not just the active holder.\n   - `setAccount` keeps the saved roles when an existing account logs in again, calls `Accounts.refresh()`, updates `MineController.anonymity`, and calls `onLoginMain` if the main role is logged in.\n6. **Nav bar**:\n   - `onChangeAccount` rebuilds the tab list, creates a new Tab/PageController (the old one is disposed after the next frame), and bumps `navBarEpoch`; the main view listens and rebuilds. The controller mixin changed to `GetTickerProviderStateMixin` because a second TabController needs a second ticker.\n   - The Local tab is added to a saved order once, placed before \"mine\", with a new `navBarLocalAdded` flag.\n   - If filtering leaves no tabs, it falls back to the default order.\n7. **Partial file deleted**: `_fail` now deletes only an empty file, so saved bytes are never thrown away.\n8. **Resume checks**:\n   - The file is opened only after the response arrives.\n   - When resuming, a 200 response rewrites the file from zero, and a 206 must have a `Content-Range` start equal to the bytes on disk (otherwise the attempt is retried).\n   - A 416 counts as complete only if the total in the header equals the size on disk; otherwise the file is emptied and the attempt retried.\n   - An early clean end of stream (`received != expected`) is a retryable failure.\n9. **Cancel during backoff**: the wait is `Future.any(delay, cancelToken.whenCancel)`, and pause/cancel is checked again afterwards, so no request is sent after cancelling.\n10. **Merge window**:\n    - Completion (`isCompleted`, `mergedPath`) is saved before the m4s files are deleted.\n    - Danmaku/subtitle/comment export runs unawaited after `nextDownload()`.\n    - Start and pause are ignored for the entry being merged (`_mergingCid`).\n    - Deleting during a merge sets `_mergeDeleted`; after the merge the output and the entry folder are removed, the entry leaves the queue, and the next download starts.\n11. **Backup of local library**: `LocalLibrary.boxes`, `importAll` and `clear` are new. `GStorage` export, import, compact, close and clear now include the three boxes, and the default folder is recreated after clear or import.\n12. **Index −1**: if the current video isn't in the download list, the playlist becomes just `[entry]`.\n13. **Shared progress key**: plain files (cid 0) key their progress by `'f' + md5(path)`. When the duration is unknown, the \"already finished\" check is skipped.\n14. **Stale comments tab**: `LocalReplyPanel(key: ValueKey(path))`, and an empty widget when `localCommentsPath` is null.\n15. **Quick-favourite**: a tap toggles only the default folder; other folders keep the item.\n16. **Fav count**: local favourites no longer change the public favourite count.\n17. **Open with while running**: `windows/runner/main.cpp` now sends an existing file path to the running instance as `librepili-open:<full path>`, using app_links' WM_COPYDATA ID. `PiliScheme` listens on `stringLinkStream`, handles that prefix with `LocalPlayer.open`, and otherwise parses the URI as before. The native change was needed: app_links' `GetLink` rejects `C:\\…` paths because its scheme regex needs at least two characters, so nothing reached Dart at all.\n18. **Dialog controller**: the folder-name dialog is now a StatefulWidget that owns and disposes its controller.\n19. **XML danmaku**: `ctime` uses `Int64(int.tryParse(p[4]) ?? 0)`.\n20. **File name**: truncation counts code points, so an emoji is never split, and the limit dropped from 120 to 80.\n\n## 2. `git diff`\n\n```diff\ndiff --git a/lib/pages/common/common_intro_controller.dart b/lib/pages/common/common_intro_controller.dart\nindex a1a1a6c63..b28560e00 100644\n--- a/lib/pages/common/common_intro_controller.dart\n+++ b/lib/pages/common/common_intro_controller.dart\n@@ -215,12 +215,8 @@ mixin FavMixin on TripleMixin {\n     }\n   }\n \n-  void _onLocalFavChanged(bool fav) {\n-    if (hasFav.value != fav) {\n-      updateFavCount(fav ? 1 : -1);\n-      hasFav.value = fav;\n-    }\n-  }\n+  // device-local only: the public favorite count is left as is\n+  void _onLocalFavChanged(bool fav) => hasFav.value = fav;\n \n   Future<void> _localFav(BuildContext context, bool isLongPress) async {\n     final key = localFavKey;\n@@ -231,14 +227,17 @@ mixin FavMixin on TripleMixin {\n     }\n     // quick fav: tap toggles the default folder, long press picks folders\n     if (enableQuickFav && !isLongPress) {\n-      final fav = !LocalLibrary.isFav(key);\n-      await LocalLibrary.setFolders(\n-        key,\n-        data,\n-        fav ? {LocalLibrary.defaultFolderId} : {},\n-      );\n-      _onLocalFavChanged(fav);\n-      SmartDialog.showToast(fav ? '已加入本地收藏' : '已取消本地收藏');\n+      // only the default folder; other folders keep the item\n+      final folders = {...LocalLibrary.foldersOf(key)};\n+      final add = !folders.contains(LocalLibrary.defaultFolderId);\n+      if (add) {\n+        folders.add(LocalLibrary.defaultFolderId);\n+      } else {\n+        folders.remove(LocalLibrary.defaultFolderId);\n+      }\n+      await LocalLibrary.setFolders(key, data, folders);\n+      _onLocalFavChanged(folders.isNotEmpty);\n+      SmartDialog.showToast(add ? '已加入本地收藏' : '已取消本地收藏');\n       return;\n     }\n     if (!enableQuickFav && isLongPress) return;\ndiff --git a/lib/pages/local/fav_sheet.dart b/lib/pages/local/fav_sheet.dart\nindex 9b409a321..3f76be627 100644\n--- a/lib/pages/local/fav_sheet.dart\n+++ b/lib/pages/local/fav_sheet.dart\n@@ -23,13 +23,39 @@ Future<String?> showFolderNameDialog(\n   String title = '新建收藏夹',\n   String initial = '',\n }) {\n-  final controller = TextEditingController(text: initial);\n   return showDialog<String>(\n     context: context,\n-    builder: (context) => AlertDialog(\n-      title: Text(title),\n+    builder: (context) => _FolderNameDialog(title: title, initial: initial),\n+  );\n+}\n+\n+/// Owns its text controller, so it is disposed with the dialog (after the\n+/// closing animation) instead of when the dialog is popped.\n+class _FolderNameDialog extends StatefulWidget {\n+  const _FolderNameDialog({required this.title, required this.initial});\n+\n+  final String title;\n+  final String initial;\n+\n+  @override\n+  State<_FolderNameDialog> createState() => _FolderNameDialogState();\n+}\n+\n+class _FolderNameDialogState extends State<_FolderNameDialog> {\n+  late final _controller = TextEditingController(text: widget.initial);\n+\n+  @override\n+  void dispose() {\n+    _controller.dispose();\n+    super.dispose();\n+  }\n+\n+  @override\n+  Widget build(BuildContext context) {\n+    return AlertDialog(\n+      title: Text(widget.title),\n       content: TextField(\n-        controller: controller,\n+        controller: _controller